  <p class="kicker"><time datetime="2026-10-04">4 October 2026</time> · Open risk, not an incident</p>
  <h1>Dependencies we can see, and two we can't yet</h1>
  <p class="deck">
    This site lists every credential and registration that can take it down. Two entries still can't be checked.
    That's the point of this note.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <ul class="updates">
    <li><time datetime="2026-10-04">4 Oct 2026</time>: written with both gaps open.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/reliability/#limits">dependency board</a> on the reliability page lists everything this site depends
    on that expires, and what breaks if it does, so each one is renewed before anyone feels it. Every day it reads each
    expiry from the service that issued it. Four entries are green: the domain, the scheduled job's GitHub token, the
    incident desk token and the log backfill token. Two are not. The usage feed token isn't set, so its row says
    "Unchecked" and today's free-tier allowance says "Not connected". The Cloudflare deploy token's expiry hasn't been
    reported yet, so its row says "Not recorded".
  </p>
  <p>
    Neither gap stops the site today, and neither is an incident. Left alone, each is a P3 risk, and the daily check
    will open a P3 reminder for it. Done means the usage feed is connected and its figures are live, and the deploy
    pipeline reports its token's expiry every day.
  </p>

  <h2>Why this sits on the reliability page</h2>
  <p>
    Objectives answer one question: is the site meeting its targets? They can't answer another: what will stop it
    while the outside probe is still green? On 2 October the site <a href="/notes/postmortem-free-tier-writes/">ran out
    of its daily database writes</a>. The limit was real and published, but nothing on the page showed it coming. The
    dependency board is the answer to that: list what can lapse, read its date, and say plainly when a date can't be
    read.
  </p>

  <h2>Current state</h2>
  <p class="muted small">Copied from the live board on 4 October 2026, 5:58 p.m. Toronto time.</p>
