  <h2>Blast radius and severity</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Usage feed missing.</strong> Visitors are served and the probe stays green, but I can't see how much of the
    day's free allowance is used. That's the same class of failure as the write-budget outage: a limit I can't see
    until it stops something. Priority: a scheduled fix this week, not a page.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Deploy token not reported.</strong> The only risk is that a deploy fails on the day the token expires,
    without warning. The live site keeps running either way. Priority: pipeline hygiene.
  </p>
  <p>
    The rule both follow: an expiry nobody could read is shown as a risk, never as OK. Each dependency gets a reminder
    at 90, 60 and 30 days, with priority rising as the date nears.
  </p>

  <h2>Findings and actions</h2>
  <div class="scroll"><table class="findings">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">#</th><th scope="col">Finding</th><th scope="col">Action</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1</td><td>The usage feed token isn't set</td><td>Add a read-only analytics token, so today's allowance is shown and its expiry is read</td><td>Open (owner)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2</td><td>The deploy token's expiry isn't reported</td><td>Add the report secret, then run the daily check once, so the pipeline reports the date every day</td><td>Open (owner)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3</td><td>The gap was visible on the page but not written down</td><td>This note, linked from the board</td><td>Done</td></tr>
    </tbody>
