  <h2>What happens next</h2>
  <p>
    I'll close both gaps this week, and record each one under "Updates" above, with the date it turned green. If I ever
    want evidence of how the board behaves when a feed goes dark, that will be a planned game day under its own name,
    like <a href="/notes/postmortem-game-day-1/">game day 1</a>. It won't be an incident.
  </p>

  <h2>What this is not</h2>
  <p>
    It isn't a configuration database, and it isn't a claim about anyone else's estate. It's one owner-operated site on
    a free tier, with six things that can expire, run in public.
  </p>

  <h2>The rule that came out of it</h2>
  <p>If the site can't read an expiry or a quota, the page says so. Silence is a bug.</p>

